<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="263d1984">&lt;p&gt;
    The Sprint Burndown Chart displays all of the work planned for a sprint against the duration of the sprint and can be
    plotted via either a bar chart or a dual line graph. Both relay the amount of work left (vertical, Y axis) in the
    sprint via either story point estimates, ideal days or tasks&amp;nbsp;on any given day (horizontal, X axis). Actual work
    completed and planned work are both plotted to show actual progress as compared to progress originally anticipated at
    the start of the sprint.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Sprint Burndown Charts Plotted with Story Points
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &amp;nbsp; &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../practice.mgmt.proj.agile_pm.base/guidances/examples/./resources/SprintBurndownChart_StoryPts_example.jpg&quot; width=&quot;700&quot; height=&quot;421&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../practice.mgmt.proj.agile_pm.base/guidances/examples/./resources/SprintBurndownChart_StoryPts_example2.jpg&quot; width=&quot;600&quot; height=&quot;366&quot; /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    Sprint Burndown Charts Plotted with Hours
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &amp;nbsp; &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../practice.mgmt.proj.agile_pm.base/guidances/examples/./resources/SprintBurndownChart_example.jpg&quot; width=&quot;700&quot; height=&quot;421&quot; /&gt;
